[h1]Speculative Markets â€” CMF Compatibility[/h1]
Use this optional patch when playing with Speculative Markets and Community Mod Framework.

It restores the Finance button and window while preserving CMF's custom sidebar buttons. Opening Finance, another CMF window, or a normal game panel closes the previous window cleanly.

[h2]Required mods and load order[/h2]
Enable these in order, with this patch below CMF and your chosen Speculative Markets channel:
[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3385002128]Community Mod Framework[/url]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3831434383]Speculative Markets[/url] or [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3839275304]Speculative Markets - Beta[/url] â€” enable one, never both
[*]Speculative Markets â€” CMF Compatibility
[/list]

Compatibility patch version 1.0.1 is built for Speculative Markets 1.0.2, CMF 1.67.6, and Victoria 3 1.15.1. CMF and one Speculative Markets channel are required. This patch changes only the interface; it does not change balance or economic mechanics.

The beta is a complete alternative to stable, not an add-on. This patch has also been tested with Beta 1.0.2-beta.2. Enable CMF and exactly one Speculative Markets channel, then manually put this patch last. A future beta that changes the interface may need an updated patch.

Finance is the large sidebar button below Power Bloc. If you do not use CMF, use Speculative Markets on its own.

[h2]Credits[/h2]
Based on the sidebar implementations from Speculative Markets and Community Mod Framework by the Victoria 3 Modding Co-op. This is a separate compatibility patch.

[h2]Morgenroete[/h2]
Using Morgenroete? Add our [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3839705018]Morgenroete compatibility patch[/url] after Morgenroete and Speculative Markets, then put the CMF patch last. Disable the older Speculative Markets+Morgenroete bridge.
